<title>UK: PowerGen falls after German bid report.</title>
<headline>PowerGen falls after German bid report.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>PowerGen Plc shares dropped on Wednesday after a Financial Times report that the UK generating company was considering a bid for Berliner Kraft-und Licht (BEWAG) AG, to be privatised early next year.</p>
<p>The purchase of part of the Berlin utility would cost PowerGen 2.5 billion marks and would be the first move for the UK company into the distribution and supply of electricity, the FT said.</p>
<p>PowerGen shares were down 4-1/2p at 568-1/2 by 0959 GMT in thin volume of 14,878 shares.  </p>
<p>No-one at PowerGen was immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5106</p>
</text>
